From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:46:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: renew the device's token during a session, and
 answer a refused user token.

The service read the device's STS token once, at start, and handed it to every connection: a
game that ran past its expiry got failures from then on. Each token request and license query now
asks for the token, renewed when it is about to expire, one request at a time. When Microsoft
refuses to exchange the user's token without interaction, the request gets an empty answer and
the log a warning that the account may need signing in again, instead of a panic.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: service-lifecycle
